  "funFact": "The sea pig (Scotoplanes globosa) is actually a sea cucumber — a deep-sea echinoderm that crawls along the ocean floor on water-filled tube feet. Despite looking nothing alike, sea pigs and sea urchins are both echinoderms, sharing the same water vascular system and calcite skeleton. The cuttlefish is a mollusc, more closely related to snails and octopuses than to any echinoderm.",
